    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"p3a_title\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## A — Missing-station penalty\\n\\nv27 MR=0.5 masked vs v27 MR=0 (all stations visible).\\n\\n*How much does removing the target station's observations hurt\\nperformance?* Both curves use the same model weights — the only\\ndifference is whether the station's own observations are available.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"p3a\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, NV, figsize=(17, 3.4))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for vi, (ax, v) in enumerate(zip(axes, VARS)):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    m27_msk = C.metric(AGG5[\\\"v27\\\"], \\\"mae\\\", sub=\\\"msk\\\", pool=(\\\"N\\\",))[:, vi]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    m27_mr0 = C.metric(AGG[\\\"v27\\\"], \\\"mae\\\", pool=(\\\"N\\\",))[:, vi]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.plot(range(1, K), m27_msk[1:], \\\"s-\\\", ms=3, lw=1.3, color=COL_MASKED,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label=\\\"MAE Tr. MR=0.5 (masked stations)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.plot(range(1, K), m27_mr0[1:], \\\"o-\\\", ms=3, lw=1.3, color=COL_VISIBLE,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label=\\\"MAE Tr. MR=0 (all visible)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_xticks(range(1, K, 2))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_xticklabels(LEAD[1::2], rotation=45, ha=\\\"right\\\", fontsize=6.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title(f\\\"{v}  [{C.UNITS[v]}]\\\", fontsize=10); ax.grid(alpha=.3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].set_ylabel(\\\"MAE [phys]\\\"); axes[-1].legend(fontsize=6.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig.suptitle(\\\"Missing-station penalty — same weights, different information\\\", y=1.04)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout(); C.save_fig(fig, \\\"43_missing_station_penalty\\\"); plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"p3b_title\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## B — Operational comparison: v27 MR=0.5 masked vs v31 MR=0\\n\\n**Not a controlled training ablation** — the evaluation conditions differ\\n(v27 has 50 % of stations removed; v31 sees all). This shows what happens\\noperationally when a masking-trained model faces actual station outages\\ncompared to a dense-trained model in ideal conditions.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"p3b\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, NV, figsize=(17, 3.4))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for vi, (ax, v) in enumerate(zip(axes, VARS)):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    m27_msk = C.metric(AGG5[\\\"v27\\\"], \\\"mae\\\", sub=\\\"msk\\\", pool=(\\\"N\\\",))[:, vi]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    m31_all = C.metric(AGG[\\\"v31\\\"], \\\"mae\\\", pool=(\\\"N\\\",))[:, vi]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    m27_all = C.metric(AGG[\\\"v27\\\"], \\\"mae\\\", pool=(\\\"N\\\",))[:, vi]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.plot(range(1, K), m27_msk[1:], \\\"s-\\\", ms=3, lw=1.3, color=COL_MASKED,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label=\\\"MAE Tr. masked (MR=0.5)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.plot(range(1, K), m27_all[1:], \\\"o-\\\", ms=3, lw=1.3, color=\\\"#1F5F6B\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label=\\\"MAE Tr. all (MR=0)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.plot(range(1, K), m31_all[1:], \\\"D-\\\", ms=3, lw=1.3, color=\\\"#D9663D\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"            label=\\\"Dense (MR=0)\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_xticks(range(1, K, 2))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_xticklabels(LEAD[1::2], rotation=45, ha=\\\"right\\\", fontsize=6.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title(f\\\"{v}  [{C.UNITS[v]}]\\\", fontsize=10); ax.grid(alpha=.3)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"axes[0].set_ylabel(\\\"MAE [phys]\\\"); axes[-1].legend(fontsize=6.5)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig.suptitle(\\\"Operational comparison (different eval conditions — not a controlled ablation)\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"             y=1.04)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout(); C.save_fig(fig, \\\"43_operational_comparison\\\"); plt.show()\"\n",
    "   ],\n",
    "   \"outputs\": [],\n",
    "   \"execution_count\": null\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"interp\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Interpretation\\n\\n**Masking penalty** is largest at Δ=0 (reconstruction: masked stations\\nhave no persistence shortcut) and shrinks with lead time as temporal\\nextrapolation dominates.\\n\\n**Missing-station penalty** (plot A) isolates the information cost: same\\nmodel weights, only whether the station's own observations are available\\nchanges.\\n\\n**Operational comparison** (plot B) mixes two effects — training regime\\nand evaluation information — so should not be interpreted as a\\ncontrolled ablation. v31 has no MR=0.5 evaluation, preventing a\\ncontrolled masking-training comparison.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"a1362a5d1ede4e66\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"## Stations excluded from evaluation, by variable\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Marks every station×variable pair dropped by `DROP_SV` (see common.py) with\\n\",\n",
    "    \"an X on the map: **black** = missing in both train and test (>50%),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**white** = missing in train only (sensor added after 2021, present in\\n\",\n",
    "    \"test), **grey** = missing in test only (no such pair exists in the current\\n\",\n",
    "    \"data — kept for completeness), **orange** = present in both splits but\\n\",\n",
    "    \"excluded for a data-quality reason (BIZ/pressure, systematic sensor drift),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"not for missingness.\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"code\",\n",
    "   \"id\": \"fec542ba86684fc1\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# ── Stations excluded from evaluation, by variable ──────────────────────────\\n\",\n",
    "    \"REASON_STYLE = {\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"missing_train\\\": dict(color=\\\"white\\\",   label=\\\"missing in train only\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"missing_test\\\":  dict(color=\\\"0.6\\\",     label=\\\"missing in test only\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"missing_both\\\":  dict(color=\\\"black\\\",   label=\\\"missing in train & test\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    \\\"drift\\\":         dict(color=\\\"#E8A838\\\", label=\\\"excluded \\\\u2014 sensor drift\\\"),\\n\",\n",
    "    \"}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"COL_INCLUDED = \\\"#2E86C1\\\"  # blue for included stations\\n\",\n",
    "    \"EXCL_REASONS = C.excluded_station_variable_reasons()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# Switzerland's LV95 extent is landscape (~350 km E-W x 220 km N-S, aspect\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# ~1.6:1), but figsize height 7.5 gave each panel a portrait box — with\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# draw_dem's equal-aspect plotting, that left the map letterboxed with a\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# huge blank margin above/below it, so the legend anchored to the bottom\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# of the panel ended up far below the visible map. Shrinking the height\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# to match the map's own aspect removes that dead space.\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig, axes = plt.subplots(1, NV, figsize=(6.0 * NV, 4.6))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for vi, (ax, v) in enumerate(zip(axes, VARS)):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    draw_dem(ax, dem_bg, dem_fg, switzerland)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Find excluded stations for this variable\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    excl_abbrs = {abbr for (abbr, var), reason in EXCL_REASONS.items() if var == v}\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    is_excl = np.array([a in excl_abbrs for a in stn.abbr])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # All included stations: circles\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    incl = ~is_excl\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.scatter(stn.easting[incl], stn.northing[incl],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"               c=COL_INCLUDED, marker=\\\"o\\\", s=60,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"               edgecolors=\\\"white\\\", linewidths=0.5, zorder=5,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"               label=\\\"included\\\" if vi == 0 else None)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    # Excluded stations: X markers, coloured by reason\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    for abbr_idx in np.where(is_excl)[0]:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        abbr = stn.abbr.iloc[abbr_idx]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        reason = EXCL_REASONS.get((abbr, v), \\\"missing_both\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        style = REASON_STYLE[reason]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        ax.scatter(stn.easting.iloc[abbr_idx], stn.northing.iloc[abbr_idx],\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                   c=style[\\\"color\\\"], marker=\\\"X\\\", s=100,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                   edgecolors=\\\"0.3\\\", linewidths=0.6, zorder=6,\\n\",\n",
    "    \"                   label=style[\\\"label\\\"] if vi == 0 else None)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    ax.set_title(f\\\"{v}\\\", fontsize=12)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"# De-duplicate legend entries\\n\",\n",
    "    \"from collections import OrderedDict\\n\",\n",
    "    \"handles, labels = axes[0].get_legend_handles_labels()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"by_label = OrderedDict(zip(labels, handles))\\n\",\n",
    "    \"fig.legend(by_label.values(), by_label.keys(), loc=\\\"lower center\\\",\\n\",\n",
    "    \"           ncol=len(by_label), fontsize=9, bbox_to_anchor=(0.5, -0.06), frameon=True)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"#fig.suptitle(\\\"Station inclusion/exclusion by variable \\\\u2014 all stations\\\", y=1.02)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.tight_layout(rect=[0, 0.06, 1, 1])\\n\",\n",
    "    \"C.save_fig(fig, \\\"excluded_stations_map\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"plt.show()\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"print(\\\"Excluded station\\\\u00d7variable pairs:\\\")\\n\",\n",
    "    \"for (abbr, v), reason in sorted(EXCL_REASONS.items()):\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    print(f\\\"  {abbr:<4} {v:<12} {reason}\\\")\"\n",
